---
import LegalPage from '@/components/ui/legal-page.astro';
import { site } from '@/config/site';
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/base-layout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Terms of use" description="The terms for using the Lifio app: a personal, private journal for habits and wellbeing. Not medical advice.">
  <LegalPage eyebrow="Terms" title="Terms of use" lead="The agreement between you and us when you use Lifio. Written to be read, not skimmed past.">
    <h2>1. The agreement</h2>
    <p>
      These terms, together with our <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a>, are an agreement between you and <strong>{site.developer}</strong> (“we”, “us”)
      about the Lifio app. By installing or using Lifio you accept them. If you don’t, please don’t use the app.
    </p>

    <h2>2. Your licence to use Lifio</h2>
    <p>
      We give you a personal, non-exclusive, non-transferable licence to use Lifio on devices you own or control, in line with these terms and the terms of
      the store you got it from. Please don’t copy, modify, resell or redistribute the app, remove its notices, or try to extract its source code, except
      where the law allows it.
    </p>

    <h2>3. Not medical advice</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>Lifio is a personal journal, not a medical device.</strong> Mood, sleep, weight, heart rate, symptoms and anything else you log are for your own
      reference. Lifio does not diagnose, treat or prevent any condition, and its notes and summaries are observations, never advice.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Talk to a doctor or other qualified professional about any health concern.</li>
      <li>Never ignore professional advice, or delay seeking it, because of something shown in Lifio.</li>
      <li>In an emergency, call your local emergency number straight away.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>4. Your data, and backing it up</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>It’s yours.</strong> Everything you enter belongs to you. We claim no rights over it.</li>
      <li><strong>It stays on your phone.</strong> Lifio has no servers, so we hold no copy and cannot recover lost data.</li>
      <li>
        <strong>Backups are up to you.</strong> Use Settings → Backup & restore to keep a backup file somewhere safe. Uninstalling the app or clearing its data
        deletes everything on the phone.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>5. The stores</h2>
    <p>
      These terms are between you and us, not Google or any other store. We alone are responsible for Lifio and its support. The store’s own terms also
      apply to your download.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Changes to Lifio</h2>
    <p>
      We may improve, change or remove features over time. Planned work is shown on the <a href="/roadmap">roadmap</a>, but plans can change, and nothing on it
      is a promise of a feature or a date.
    </p>

    <h2>7. Ownership</h2>
    <p>
      The app, its design, artwork, name and logo belong to {site.developer}. Lifio includes open-source components under their own licences, listed in the
      app under Settings → About.
    </p>

    <h2>8. No warranty</h2>
    <p>
      As far as the law allows, Lifio is provided “as is” and “as available”, without warranties of any kind, including fitness for a particular purpose,
      accuracy, or uninterrupted operation. Reminders depend on your phone and may be delayed or blocked by its settings.
    </p>

    <h2>9. Limit of liability</h2>
    <p>
      As far as the law allows, we are not liable for indirect, incidental, special or consequential damages, or for loss of data, arising from your use of
      Lifio or your inability to use it. Nothing in these terms limits rights you have under consumer law that cannot be limited.
    </p>

    <h2>10. Ending the agreement</h2>
    <p>You can end this agreement at any time by uninstalling Lifio. The sections on medical information, data, ownership, warranty and liability still apply.</p>

    <h2>11. Changes to these terms</h2>
    <p>If these terms change, the new version will appear here with a new date. Using Lifio after that means you accept the new terms.</p>

    <h2>12. Contact</h2>
    <p>Questions about these terms: <a href={`mailto:${site.supportEmail}`}>{site.supportEmail}</a>.</p>
  </LegalPage>
</BaseLayout>
